@startuml
!theme plain

title P3 capture-quality v1 — one shared processor and the two ceilings
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false

package "Local capture control" {
  [Explicit local action] as Action
  [Visible + accessible\ncapture indicator] as Indicator
  [Generation / route controller] as Control
}

package "Realtime boundaries" {
  [Input device callback\ntimestamp + bounded enqueue] as CaptureCB
  [Playback render callback\npost-local-gain reference tap] as RenderCB
  [Output device] as Output
}

package "Shared capture-quality worker" {
  [Clock + 48 kHz mono\nformat alignment] as Align
  [Reference alignment\n<= 100 ms age, +/-200 ppm] as RefAlign
  [AEC] as AEC
  [Noise suppression] as NS
  [Bounded input AGC\n-20 dBFS RMS target\n-3 dBFS peak ceiling] as AGC
}

package "Workflow sinks" {
  [Recorded clip\ndraft writer] as Clip
  [Five-second local\nself-test writer] as SelfTest
  [Live PTT\nOpus encoder] as Live
}

package "Receiver playback graph — separate policy" {
  [Program + overlay +\ninterrupt + received live] as Mix
  [Post-mix limiter\n-1 dBFS ceiling] as Limiter
  [Final non-amplifying\nrecipient-local volume] as Volume
}

Action --> Indicator : preparing before device activation
Action --> Control : fresh generation + requested route
Control --> CaptureCB : open accepted/degraded-consented route
CaptureCB --> Align : timestamped native PCM
RenderCB --> RefAlign : bounded memory-only reference
Align --> RefAlign : capture clock
RefAlign --> AEC
AEC --> NS
NS --> AGC
AGC --> Clip
AGC --> SelfTest
AGC --> Live

Mix --> Limiter
Limiter --> Volume
Volume --> RenderCB : exact samples before device submission
RenderCB --> Output

Control ..> RefAlign : generation + route change resets
Control ..> Clip : exactly one selected sink
Control ..> SelfTest : exactly one selected sink
Control ..> Live : exactly one selected sink

note bottom of AGC
Input AGC cannot change the receiver ceiling.
The coordinator controls neither ceiling.
end note

note bottom of Control
Route/device change stops sample commit,
keeps the indicator visible, advances generation,
and re-arms within 1500 ms or terminates explicitly.
end note

note bottom of RenderCB
No allocation, blocking lock, I/O or logging.
Reference is never persisted or uploaded.
end note

@enduml
